      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5b4df6383c524f39e9923625",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As far as I can tell it seems to be that the view camera isn't actually anchoring to the head and instead defaults into the hips (or other root bone).\n\nIf you use an avatar with culling off (so you can see the texture from the inside) it is easier to see where it moves to.\n\nMoving around seems to shift it back into the proper place but only while moving.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5cdf8912fe052b5da3ed7191",
